        "original_id": "8d94113f-917e-5b99-b0ae-8ee51b0b037c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: G. D. Spradlin, Marlon Brando, Pat Hingle\n- Films: On the Waterfront, The Godfather, A Streetcar Named Desire, Viva Zapata!, Sayonara\n- Topics: acting credits, co-stars, award-winning performances\n\nFacts:\n- In 1951, Marlon Brando performed in the film \"A Streetcar Named Desire.\"\n- In 1954, Marlon Brando won an Academy Award for his performance as Terry Malloy in \"On the Waterfront.\"\n- In 1954, \"On the Waterfront\" was Pat Hingle's first film.\n- In 1957, \"Sayonara\" was released as a Technicolor American film starring Marlon Brando in Technirama.\n- In 1972, Marlon Brando won an Academy Award for his performance as Vito Corleone in \"The Godfather.\"\n- Marlon Brando also performed in the film \"Viva Zapata!\"\n- G. D. Spradlin was credited in more than 70 television and film productions.\n- G. D. Spradlin performed alongside actors including Marlon Brando, Al Pacino, Charlton Heston, George C. Scott, and Johnny Depp.",
